TUDOR TIMES WEEKLY =E2=80=94 week of 19 April 1543
Your trusted source for crown, court and countryside.

THIS WEEK IN HISTORY:
  * The warship Mary Rose sank in the Solent in 1545 and was raised again in =
1982.
  * The Dissolution of the Monasteries (1536-1541) transferred vast monastic =
wealth to the Crown.
  * Cardinal Wolsey rose from humble beginnings to become the second most pow=
erful man in England.

COURT WHISPERS: New French fashions arrive at Greenwich =E2=80=94 ruffs are s=
aid to be growing.

WEATHER: Grey, with a chance of beheadings. (Editorial humour; no offence int=
ended.)

